Let me write solutions for each task in Wochu.

**t0-count**: Read n, print 1..n.

```
weltuxle n := leidush(lono());
keit (weltuxle i := 1; i <= n; i := i + 1) {
    leshdei i;
}
```

Wait — leidush(lono()) — lono returns a string, leidush converts. Fine.

**t0-day-names**: Loop reading lines until leitchux. Use yishzit or if-else.

```
weltuxle line := lono();
krenul (line <> leitchux) {
    weltuxle n := leidush(line);
    nei (n == 1) { leshdei "Monday"; }
    ...
    wogeish { leshdei "invalid"; }
    line := lono();
}
```

**t0-even-odd**: Count evens/odds. Negative numbers: yeil follows rounding-toward-positive-infinity division. a - b*(a/b). For negative a: e.g., -7 / 2 = -3, so -7 yeil 2 = -7 - 2*(-3) = -1. So -7 yeil 2 = -1, not 0. So use absolute value or compute differently. Better: use n yeil 2 == 0 but for negatives: -8 / 2 = -4, -8 yeil 2 = -8 -2*(-4)=0. -7 yeil 2 = -1. So even check works: even iff n yeil 2 == 0. Odd iff n yeil 2 == 1 or -1. Simplest: check n yeil 2 == 0 for even, else odd. Since every integer is even or odd regardless. So:

```
weltuxle even := 0;
weltuxle odd := 0;
weltuxle line := lono();
krenul (line <> leitchux) {
    weltuxle n := leidush(line);
    nei (n yeil 2 == 0) { even := even + 1; } wogeish { odd := odd + 1; }
    line := lono();
}
leshdei "even " + even;
leshdei "odd " + odd;
```

