```

**t0-reverse-lines**: Read lines into a list, then print in reverse.

```
weltuxle lines := [];
weltuxle line := lono();
krenul (line <> leitchux) {
    koshkil(lines, line);
    line := lono();
}
weltuxle i := dushzosh(lines);
krenul (i > 0) {
    i := i - 1;
    leshdei lines[i];
}
```

All good. Check syntax: statements end with `;`. leshdei inside branches fine. `weltuxle i := dushzosh(lines);` fine.

One check on count: leidush accepts surrounding spaces and leading '-', returns int. Good.

For fizzbuzz condition precedence: `i yeil 15 == 0` — yeil binds tighter than ==, so (i yeil 15) == 0. Good.

